# The Node version is pinned per project, not globally.
#
# A concrete reason: rolldown (the engine behind Vite 8 and Vitest 4) requires
# ^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0. On Node 20.18 npm SILENTLY skips the native binding as not satisfying
# `engines`, the install succeeds, and the tests only blow up at run time with "Cannot find native
# binding" — a message that points at npm rather than at the Node version.
nodejs 22.14.0
